Own private, `gcBindMemory`-bound collector state, never wired through
`stwBind`/`worldBind`. Every assertion this program makes — `naiveShort`,
`exactMatch`, and the started/joined/released bits — is read out of that
private heap's own object count (`gcNumObjects`/`gcNumObjectsExact`,
`../thread/allocmigrate`) or off the thread-provider handles, never out of
anything the AMBIENT collector scans or sweeps. Whether the ambient
collector ran 0 times or 100,000 times cannot move any of those numbers —
same reasoning as `../gcslotbitmap`'s own `no-collect`.
